  "$id": "https://agent-braid.dev/specs/061-activity-viewer/contracts/loom-event.schema.json",
  "title": "agent-braid-loom/v0.1 event (draft contract, not adopted)",
  "description": "One line of a Loom event stream (JSON Lines, at most 16 KiB per line, seq strictly increasing). A file or POST body holding more than 50000 events is refused; the live in-memory ring instead evicts the oldest events and announces each evicted range with a ring-evicted gap. Planned contract of SPEC-061; no implementation exists. Every event is read-only: executionAuthorization is the constant false. compatibilityClass is the Article 13 class (0 heuristic to 5 Yang-Baxter) declared by the analysis fact the event carries, or null when the event carries no per-pair analysis result (analysis.report, strands, effort, gaps, session); it is never a guarantee and never a safety ordering. Status and mode enums are copied verbatim from their source contracts. Effort figures are host estimates kept in memory. Duplicate JSON members and non-finite numbers are refused before schema validation.",
